{
  "verdict": "NOT ADOPTED (2026-11). Over 10 years including delisted issues, 'cheap + improving quarterly OP' does not raise the share of stocks that double and its excess return is ~0 for 2016-12..2021-11; the strong result of the earlier 5-year study came from the 2021-12+ value rally. What holds in every year is fewer large losses: cheap stocks fall 30%+ far less often. Cheap minus expensive was negative in 2017-2019 (Prime clearly).",
  "method": "- Month-end formation, 12-month forward price return (no dividends). An issue delisted inside the\n  window is closed at its last traded price, so delisted issues are not dropped (no survivor bias).\n- Market at formation from the snapshot of that month: TSE 1st -> Prime, TSE 2nd / JASDAQ Standard ->\n  Standard, Mothers / JASDAQ Growth -> Growth. Only common stock (product category 011, 4-char codes).\n- Universe: price >= 100 yen; 20-day median turnover >= 10M yen (Standard + Growth) or 100M (Prime).\n- B/P: last fiscal-year BPS (split-adjusted to the formation date) / raw close; the latest disclosure\n  must be <= 200 days old. Quarterly OP yoy: stand-alone quarter vs the same quarter a year earlier\n  (both positive base). Disclosures at/after 15:00 count from the next day.\n- Rule: B/P rank >= 60th percentile and quarterly OP yoy rank >= 70th percentile within the month.",
  "formation_months": [
    "2016-11",
    "2025-10"
  ],
  "note": "q_op_yoy needs the same quarter a year earlier, so the rule has picks from about 2017-11 only.",
